IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-convention-scope`

-- Tests for the Convention, Chapters I and II (Articles 1 to 16, and 34), each against the
-- Convention it names.  Every expectation is read off the text of the Article in the Schedule
-- named beside it.  Positional construction with OF; the ruler above each block names the
-- columns.  A rule for which one of the three texts has no provision is asserted REFUSED.

§ `Tests -- Chapters I and II`

§§ `Articles 1, 2 and 34. Scope`

-- Carriage Facts: persons/baggage/cargo, by aircraft, for reward, gratuitous by an air transport
-- undertaking, places in two High Contracting Parties, places in one High Contracting Party,
-- agreed stopping place in another State, performed by the State or a public body, performed
-- directly by the State, the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol, postal,
-- experimental trial, extraordinary circumstances.
`an international carriage for reward` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`carriage within one State with no stopping place abroad` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`carriage within one State with an agreed stopping place abroad` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`gratuitous international carriage by an air transport undertaking` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`gratuitous international carriage by a private person` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`international carriage by road` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`international carriage performed directly by the State` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the same, where the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`international carriage of mail` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an experimental trial flight` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`carriage in extraordinary circumstances` MEANS `Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the carriage is international carriage` `an international carriage for reward`
#ASSERT NOT `the carriage is international carriage` `carriage within one State with no stopping place abroad`
#ASSERT `the carriage is international carriage` `carriage within one State with an agreed stopping place abroad`

#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `an international carriage for reward`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `an international carriage for reward`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `an international carriage for reward`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `carriage within one State with no stopping place abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `carriage within one State with no stopping place abroad`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `carriage within one State with an agreed stopping place abroad`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `gratuitous international carriage by an air transport undertaking`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `gratuitous international carriage by an air transport undertaking`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `gratuitous international carriage by a private person`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `international carriage by road`
-- Article 2(1): State carriage is within the Convention, unless the Additional Protocol is availed of
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `international carriage performed directly by the State`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `international carriage performed directly by the State`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `the same, where the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the same, where the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the same, where the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol`
-- Article 2(2): postal carriage
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `international carriage of mail`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `international carriage of mail`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `international carriage of mail`
-- Article 34: the Second Schedule takes experimental and extraordinary carriage out altogether; the others take out only the documents
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `an experimental trial flight`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `an experimental trial flight`
#ASSERT NOT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT `the Convention applies to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `the provisions on documents of carriage apply to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `the provisions on documents of carriage apply to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `the provisions on documents of carriage apply to the carriage` `the Warsaw Convention` `carriage in extraordinary circumstances`
#ASSERT `the provisions on documents of carriage apply to the carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `an international carriage for reward`

-- Article 1(3): successive carriage.  Successive Carriage Facts: several successive carriers,
-- regarded as a single operation, one contract or series performed wholly within one State.
#ASSERT `the carriage is one undivided carriage` (`Successive Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carriage is one undivided carriage` (`Successive Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carriage is one undivided carriage` (`Successive Carriage Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the undivided carriage keeps its international character` (`Successive Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the undivided carriage keeps its international character` (`Successive Carriage Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)

-- Article 2(2) and (3) (Third Schedule): the carrier of postal items is liable only to the postal administration
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `international carriage of mail`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `an international carriage for reward`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` `the Warsaw Convention` `international carriage of mail`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `international carriage of mail`

§§ `Article 3. Passenger ticket`

-- Ticket Facts: delivered, place and date of issue, places of departure and destination, agreed stopping places,
-- name and address of the carrier, statement of liability rules, single-Party-with-stopping-place condition,
-- stopping place indicated, the Warsaw notice, accepted the passenger without a ticket.
`a complete Warsaw ticket` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a complete Hague ticket` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a Hague ticket that should indicate a stopping place but does not` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a Hague ticket that indicates the stopping place` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a passenger accepted without a ticket` MEANS `Ticket Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw ticket`
#ASSERT NOT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Warsaw ticket`
#ASSERT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Hague ticket`
#ASSERT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a complete Hague ticket`
#ASSERT NOT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Hague ticket`
#ASSERT NOT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague ticket that should indicate a stopping place but does not`
#ASSERT `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague ticket that indicates the stopping place`

#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger accepted without a ticket` EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a passenger accepted without a ticket` EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a passenger accepted without a ticket` EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
-- a ticket that lacks the notice: forfeits Article 22 under the First and Third Schedules, nothing under the Second
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw ticket` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Warsaw ticket` EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a complete Warsaw ticket` EQUALS `Article 22 is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the passenger ticket forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Hague ticket` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the passenger ticket affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`
#ASSERT `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention`
#ASSERT `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` `the Warsaw Convention`

§§ `Article 4. Baggage check`

-- Baggage Check Facts: other than small personal objects, delivered, in duplicate, place and date, places, carriers' names,
-- ticket number, statement of delivery to the bearer, number and weight of packages, declared value, liability statement,
-- combined with a compliant passenger ticket, single-Party-with-stopping-place condition, stopping place indicated,
-- the Warsaw notice, the carrier took charge without a check.
`a complete Warsaw baggage check` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Warsaw baggage check without the ticket number` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`no baggage check, the carrier took charge` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`small personal objects with no check` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Hague baggage check with the notice` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a Hague baggage check without the notice` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a baggage check combined with a compliant ticket` MEANS `Baggage Check Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw baggage check`
#ASSERT NOT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw baggage check without the ticket number`
#ASSERT NOT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `no baggage check, the carrier took charge`
#ASSERT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `small personal objects with no check`
#ASSERT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague baggage check with the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague baggage check without the notice`
#ASSERT `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a baggage check combined with a compliant ticket`

#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw baggage check` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw baggage check without the ticket number` EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `no baggage check, the carrier took charge` EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `small personal objects with no check` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague baggage check with the notice` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague baggage check without the notice` EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a Hague baggage check without the notice` EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a baggage check combined with a compliant ticket` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the baggage check forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `no baggage check, the carrier took charge` EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the baggage check affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`

§§ `Articles 5 to 9. Air waybill and documentation relating to cargo`

-- Waybill Facts: made out, three parts, first part, second part, third part, signed on acceptance, signed before loading,
-- then the particulars (a) place and date, (b) places, (c) stopping places, (d) consignor, (e) first carrier, (f) consignee,
-- (g) nature, (h) packages, (i) weight and volume, (j) apparent condition, (k) freight, (l) price on delivery, (m) declared
-- value, (n) number of parts, (o) documents, (p) time and route, (q) liability statement, then the stopping-place condition,
-- stopping place indicated, the Warsaw notice, the weight of the consignment, another means substituted, accepted without.
`a complete Warsaw waybill` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Warsaw waybill without the weight and volume` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Warsaw waybill without the apparent condition` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo accepted without an air waybill` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a Hague waybill with the notice` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Hague waybill without the notice` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a waybill that should indicate a stopping place but does not` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Montreal waybill with the weight` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Montreal waybill without the weight` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`another means substituted` MEANS `Waybill Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw waybill without the weight and volume`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw waybill without the apparent condition`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill`
#ASSERT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague waybill with the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague waybill without the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a waybill that should indicate a stopping place but does not`
#ASSERT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a Montreal waybill with the weight`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a Montreal waybill without the weight`

-- Article 9: what a missing or defective air waybill forfeits, under each Schedule
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw waybill without the weight and volume` EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
-- Article 9 (Second Schedule) forfeits only for the lack of particulars (a) to (i) and (q); the apparent condition is (j)
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Warsaw waybill without the apparent condition` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo accepted without an air waybill` EQUALS `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo accepted without an air waybill` EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo accepted without an air waybill` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague waybill with the notice` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague waybill without the notice` EQUALS `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
#ASSERT `what the air waybill forfeits` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a Montreal waybill without the weight` EQUALS `nothing is forfeited`
#ASSERT NOT `the absence, irregularity or loss of the air waybill affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage`

-- Article 6: the parts and signatures
#ASSERT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill`
#ASSERT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a Hague waybill with the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw Convention` `a Hague waybill with the notice`
#ASSERT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a Montreal waybill with the weight`
#ASSERT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a complete Warsaw waybill`
#ASSERT NOT `the air waybill complies with Article 6` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo accepted without an air waybill`

-- Article 5
#ASSERT `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` `the Warsaw Convention`
#ASSERT `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`
#ASSERT `another means of preserving the record may be substituted for an air waybill` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `another means substituted`
#ASSERT NOT `another means of preserving the record may be substituted for an air waybill` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo accepted without an air waybill`
#ASSERT REFUSED `another means of preserving the record may be substituted for an air waybill` `the Warsaw Convention` `another means substituted`
#ASSERT REFUSED `another means of preserving the record may be substituted for an air waybill` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `another means substituted`
#ASSERT NOT `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` `the Warsaw Convention`

-- Article 6(5) and Article 6(4)
#ASSERT `the carrier is deemed to have made out the air waybill on behalf of the consignor` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is deemed to have made out the air waybill on behalf of the consignor` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is deemed to have made out the air waybill on behalf of the consignor` FALSE FALSE

-- Article 7
#ASSERT `the carrier may require the consignor to make out separate air waybills` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier may require the consignor to make out separate air waybills` FALSE
#ASSERT `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` TRUE `another means substituted`
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` FALSE `another means substituted`
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` TRUE `cargo accepted without an air waybill`
