§§ `Articles 10 and 11. Responsibility for particulars; evidence`

-- Indemnity Facts: damage suffered by the carrier, by another person, carrier liable to that person, by reason of the
-- consignor's particulars, by reason of the carrier's particulars, damage suffered by the consignor.
`the carrier's own damage from the consignor's particulars` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`another person's damage, the carrier not liable to that person` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`another person's damage, the carrier liable to that person` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`damage not caused by the consignor's particulars` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the consignor's damage from the carrier's particulars` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`the consignor's damage from his own particulars` MEANS `Indemnity Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw Convention` `the carrier's own damage from the consignor's particulars`
#ASSERT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw Convention` `another person's damage, the carrier not liable to that person`
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `another person's damage, the carrier not liable to that person`
#ASSERT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `another person's damage, the carrier liable to that person`
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `another person's damage, the carrier not liable to that person`
#ASSERT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `another person's damage, the carrier liable to that person`
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor is liable for the damage` `the Warsaw Convention` `damage not caused by the consignor's particulars`
#ASSERT `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the consignor's damage from the carrier's particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the consignor's damage from his own particulars`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` `the Warsaw Convention` `the consignor's damage from the carrier's particulars`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the consignor's damage from the carrier's particulars`

#ASSERT `the air waybill or the receipt for the cargo is prima facie evidence of the conclusion of the contract, of the receipt or acceptance of the cargo and of the conditions of carriage`

-- Article 11(2): Statement Facts: kind, checked in the consignor's presence and stated, apparent condition
#ASSERT `the statement is evidence against the carrier` (`Statement Facts` OF `a statement of the weight, dimensions or packing of the cargo, or the number of packages`, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the statement is evidence against the carrier` (`Statement Facts` OF `a statement of the quantity, volume or condition of the cargo`, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the statement is evidence against the carrier` (`Statement Facts` OF `a statement of the quantity, volume or condition of the cargo`, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is evidence against the carrier` (`Statement Facts` OF `a statement of the quantity, volume or condition of the cargo`, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `Articles 12 to 16. Disposition, delivery and customs`

-- Disposition Facts: the consignee's right has begun, declines to accept, cannot be communicated with, carrier obeyed the
-- consignor without requiring production of the part, damage to a person lawfully in possession, impossible to carry out
-- the orders, the carrier informed the consignor forthwith.
#ASSERT `the consignor has the right of disposition` (`Disposition Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the consignor has the right of disposition` (`Disposition Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the consignor has the right of disposition` (`Disposition Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the consignor has the right of disposition` (`Disposition Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable for the damage caused by obeying the consignor's orders` (`Disposition Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable for the damage caused by obeying the consignor's orders` (`Disposition Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable for the damage caused by obeying the consignor's orders` (`Disposition Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

#TRACE `the carrier's duty to inform the consignor that his orders cannot be carried out` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The carrier` DOES `inform the consignor of the impossibility of carrying out his orders` AT 0

#TRACE `the carrier's duty to give the consignee notice of the arrival of the cargo` AT 0 WITH
